# cached upstream data — regenerate with scripts/fetch_osm.py
data/raw/
data/interim/
data/processed/*

# The generated distance matrices are deliberately NOT committed. They are a
# Derivative Database of OpenStreetMap and carry ODbL, which is not ours to
# waive — committing them would put a second licence in a repository that ships
# GPLv3 in totality. See data/processed/taxi_distance/ODbL-NOTICE.md, which is
# committed because it is our own documentation rather than OSM-derived data.
!data/processed/taxi_distance/
data/processed/taxi_distance/*
!data/processed/taxi_distance/README.md
!data/processed/taxi_distance/ODbL-NOTICE.md

# Challenge datasets: never commit, and not redistributable under any licence.
# Supplied under the terms of the challenge, which grant access to participants
# and nothing further. Only the README explaining where they go is tracked.
*.parquet
challenge_data/
data/challenge/*
!data/challenge/README.md

# Submission files and the manifest written beside each one. The parquet is
# already covered by *.parquet; the manifest is JSON and would not be. What the
# record needs from a manifest goes into reports/ through the script that reads
# it, so nothing in this directory is ever committed by a stray `git add`.
data/submissions/

# Assistant configuration and instructions. The repository carries no trace of
# what wrote it, and these are the two paths that would carry one: neither was
# ignored, so `git add -A` would have committed the local settings file against
# that rule. scripts/check_licence_hygiene.py lists both as forbidden as well,
# so removing these two lines fails the gate rather than passing quietly.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# credentials — Minio/OpenSky bucket keys
.env
*.env
secrets.toml
credentials*

# CatBoost writes its training log into the working directory whenever the
# booster falls back to it, which happens wherever lightgbm is not importable.
# No test fits one, so there is no train_dir to point somewhere else.
catboost_info/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# os
.DS_Store
